WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:05.300
Godzilla: King of the Monsters is set to follow
up a film that reimagined cinema's favorite

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:09.480
fire-breathing behemoth — and left everyone
with plenty of questions, like: How does the

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.170
movie connect to its predecessors?

00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:15.480
And, is Godzilla really the king, or is he
just some scaly-ass poser?

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:18.110
Don't worry — we've got the answers you're
looking for.

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:19.110
New faces, returning stars

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:22.650
A host of stars are joining the Godzilla family
for King of the Monsters.

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:28.210
The star-studded cast includes The Conjuring
franchise veteran Vera Farmiga as paleobiologist

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:32.759
Dr. Emma Russell, Stranger Things darling
Millie Bobby Brown as Madison Russell, and

00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:37.569
Friday Night Lights alum Kyle Chandler as
animal behavior expert Dr. Mark Russell — Emma's

00:00:37.569 --> 00:00:38.569
ex-husband.

00:00:38.569 --> 00:00:42.510
Though there are more than a handful of new
characters to meet in Godzilla: King of the

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:45.309
Monsters, the film doesn't go without a few
returning favorites.

00:00:45.309 --> 00:00:49.889
The actors returning for King of the Monsters
include Ken Watanabe and Sally Hawkins.

00:00:49.889 --> 00:00:54.429
Watanabe slips back into the crisp white lab
coat of his Godzilla character Dr. Ishiro

00:00:54.429 --> 00:00:58.709
Serizawa, a scientist at the crypto-zoological
organization Monarch.

00:00:58.709 --> 00:01:03.089
Hawkins will be back as Serizawa's right-hand
woman Dr. Vivienne Graham.

00:01:03.089 --> 00:01:05.510
Another actor coming back for King of the
Monsters?

00:01:05.510 --> 00:01:06.510
Godzilla himself.

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:07.790
Professional stuntman T.J.

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:12.420
Storm reprises the monstrous role in a motion-capture
performance.

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:20.280
Family, rescue, and monsters

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:24.640
The vast majority of sequels use the ending
of their direct precursors as a springboard

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:26.880
to launch into new narrative territory.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:29.200
Godzilla: King of the Monsters is no exception.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:35.170
Set in 2019, five years after 2014's Godzilla,
King of the Monsters centers around the members

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:40.070
of Monarch as they go head to head with a
"battery of god-sized monsters" — and by

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:45.420
that, we mean Godzilla and his three foes
Rodan, Ghidorah, and Mothra.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:49.620
Mankind once believed the "ancient super-species,"
collectively known as Titans, were the stuff

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:50.620
of fiction.

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:54.420
The Titans are all too real — and threaten
humanity's existence when they rise to fight

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:55.480
for dominance.

00:01:55.480 --> 00:02:00.010
Godzilla: King of the Monsters also sees Dr.
Emma Russell and her daughter Madison get

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:05.060
kidnapped by a mysterious organization that
wants to use Emma's intellect and inventiveness,

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:09.369
as well as Madison's "strange connection"
with Mothra, for nefarious purposes.

00:02:09.369 --> 00:02:14.129
Emma feels humans and Titans can co-exist
peacefully, but after experiencing a great

00:02:14.129 --> 00:02:15.879
loss, her ex-husband Mark doesn't agree.

00:02:15.879 --> 00:02:20.739
Despite holding a negative view of the monsters,
Mark teams with Monarch's Dr. Ishiro Serizawa

00:02:20.739 --> 00:02:24.010
and Dr. Vivienne Graham to rescue Emma and
Madison.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:25.010
The terrible trio

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:29.019
Godzilla: King of the Monsters will bring
Mothra, Rodan, and Ghidorah back to the big

00:02:29.019 --> 00:02:32.950
screen, and we've got the skinny on who the
three creatures are and how they'll be depicted.

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:38.849
A colossal moth-like being, Mothra will be
both beautiful and deadly in King of the Monsters.

00:02:38.849 --> 00:02:42.849
Director Michael Dougherty aimed to give her
a realistic appearance, including long legs

00:02:42.849 --> 00:02:46.140
that help her fight against and defend herself
from her adversaries.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:51.079
Rodan, on the other hand, is a pterodactyl-like
monster, described by Dougherty as a "massive

00:02:51.079 --> 00:02:55.300
A-bomb [and a] bit of a rogue" with incredible
physical power.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:56.300
Dougherty elaborated:

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:59.370
"You never quite know where his loyalties
lie.

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:03.569
Godzilla's more of a lumbering, plodding presence;
it takes him a couple of days to destroy a

00:03:03.569 --> 00:03:04.810
city like Tokyo.

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:07.069
Rodan can level it without even thinking."

00:03:07.069 --> 00:03:11.690
As for Ghidorah, the three-headed dragon beast
is Godzilla's ultimate nemesis.

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:16.540
That each of his heads has "its own different
personality" — one alpha and two "lackeys"

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:20.200
— makes Ghidorah even more formidable than
Godzilla's other challengers.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:24.980
"Good thing he's on our side."

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:28.680
The title of Godzilla: King of the Monsters
tells audiences all they need to know about

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:33.489
the monster's ranking in the Titan hierarchy:
he's the big kahuna, the grand poobah, the

00:03:33.489 --> 00:03:34.489
top banana.

00:03:34.489 --> 00:03:38.019
But what about where Godzilla stands on the
hero-villain binary?

00:03:38.019 --> 00:03:42.459
As Bradley Whitford's Dr. Stanton states in
one of the film's trailers, Godzilla is on

00:03:42.459 --> 00:03:47.249
our side," and can help save mankind from
being eradicated as soon as Monarch sets him

00:03:47.249 --> 00:03:48.249
free.

00:03:48.249 --> 00:03:51.379
Though Godzilla isn't out to harm humans,
not everyone is totally willing to consider

00:03:51.379 --> 00:03:52.730
him the good guy.

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:57.359
O'Shea Jackson Jr., whose character Barnes
leads Monarch's military crew, the G-Team,

00:03:57.359 --> 00:04:00.420
told Fandango that Godzilla is a heroic protector:

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:05.250
"Speaking as a Godzilla fan, I always hated
those humans who acted like didn't Godzilla

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:06.739
didn't just save their ass.

00:04:06.739 --> 00:04:11.469
What happened in San Francisco in 2014 [in
Godzilla], from what I can see, he holds down

00:04:11.469 --> 00:04:13.260
the Pacific, so California seems safe.

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:14.400
So I'm down with that."

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:18.060
On the converse, Kyle Chandler, whose Dr.
Mark Russell has a "troubled history with

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:21.890
the Titans," isn't a fan of any of the Titans,
Godzilla included, explaining:

00:04:21.890 --> 00:04:26.530
"They're mean, ugly, dangerous, and they've
caused havoc with [Mark's] family."

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:29.310
Looks like some will be hesitant to bow down
to the king.

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:32.920
That could be their undoing... or give Godzilla
the chance to prove them wrong.

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:33.920
Past meets present

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:37.800
Godzilla: King of the Monsters may be as fresh
as can be in terms of its time setting — taking

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:42.910
place in 2019, the same year of its release
— but it also incorporates elements of the

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:43.910
past.

00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:47.750
Talking with Fandango, director Michael Dougherty
detailed that the concept of King of the Monsters

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:51.610
is rooted in the mythology that the world
belongs to the Titans, since they were on

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:53.720
Earth long before humans came along.

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:58.780
In his words, humans are "the invasive species,"
and the Titans are, quote, "the old gods…

00:04:58.780 --> 00:04:59.940
the first gods."

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:04.290
He also shared that King of the Monsters gives
the creatures, according to him, "a more mythological,

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:07.160
almost biblical, backdrop" when exploring
their history.

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:08.170
Dougherty explained:

00:05:08.170 --> 00:05:11.170
"These creatures were once worshipped by some
ancient civilization.

00:05:11.170 --> 00:05:15.330
I really love that about the old movies that
Mothra was this deity.

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:17.080
It really opened up the mythology."

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:22.080
In simple terms, King of the Monsters sees
ancient mythology clash with the modern day,

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:25.660
bringing humans and god-like beasts together
at the same point in time.

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:29.070
It's a union partially motivated by a childhood
wish of Dougherty, who said,

00:05:29.070 --> 00:05:34.150
"As a kid it, always bummed me out that dinosaurs
never actually crossed paths [with humans].

00:05:34.150 --> 00:05:35.740
So I'm saying f--- that."

00:05:35.740 --> 00:05:36.740
Filling in the gaps

00:05:36.740 --> 00:05:40.970
The five-year break between Godzilla and King
of the Monsters leaves a lot of time unaccounted

00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:41.970
for.

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:44.680
Though we can't say for certain whether King
of the Monsters will explain the in-world

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:49.680
events that went down between 2014 and 2019,
or how the film will address the gap, we can

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:52.800
assure you that another piece of Godzilla
content definitely will.

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:58.580
As of ten days ahead of King of the Monsters'
May 31st debut, fans can dig into Godzilla:

00:05:58.580 --> 00:05:59.580
Aftershock.

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:03.810
The Legendary Comics-published tie-in prequel
graphic novel takes place in the time after

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:07.890
Godzilla and before King of the Monsters and
sets the stage for the sequel.

00:06:07.890 --> 00:06:13.100
Written by Arvid Nelson with artwork by Drew
Edward Johnson, Godzilla: Aftershock continues

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:18.490
the plot laid out in Godzilla, seeing an all-new
monster, MUTO Prime, ascend from deep within

00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:22.860
the planet and Godzilla battle an "unstoppable
primal instinct" that challenges his inner

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:23.860
strength.

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:27.580
The graphic novel also introduces several
characters from King of the Monsters, as Dr.

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:31.400
Emma Russell and the members of Monarch try
to put an end to the creature and attempt

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:35.831
to piece together the truth behind a past
tragedy "of apocalyptic proportions" that

00:06:35.831 --> 00:06:37.670
is resurfacing again.

00:06:37.670 --> 00:06:42.180
As Godzilla fights in a rivalry that spans
as many years as the Earth has been a planet,

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:45.010
Emma unravels secrets beyond anyone's wildest
imagination.

00:06:45.010 --> 00:06:46.010
A meaningful message

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:50.080
King of the Monsters is about more than a
bunch of behemoths trading blows — in fact,

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:54.280
it carries a message about environmentalism,
the role humans play in the destruction of

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:58.130
planet Earth, and the importance of science
in our modern society.

00:06:58.130 --> 00:06:59.650
Director Michael Dougherty told Fandango:

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:05.090
"In a time when, in our current climate, where
science is being constantly questioned and

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:09.070
targeted, the idea of creating a film where
scientists are heroes, I thought was really

00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:10.070
important."

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:13.340
"So you want to make Godzilla our pet?"

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:15.320
"No.

00:07:15.320 --> 00:07:18.420
We would be his."

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:22.330
Star Vera Farmiga even described the movie
as being more about environmentalism than

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:25.340
your average monster-filled flick, which is
what drew her to the project.

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:26.450
An Easter egg hunt

00:07:26.450 --> 00:07:30.180
Nowadays, you'd be hard-pressed to find a
modern film that doesn't deliver fan service

00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:31.730
in the form of Easter eggs.

00:07:31.730 --> 00:07:35.710
They've become the norm in contemporary cinema,
with audiences practically squirming in their

00:07:35.710 --> 00:07:39.900
seats at the thought of finding every last
hidden secret tucked inside a new release.

00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:44.080
It should come as little surprise that Godzilla:
King of the Monsters will continue this trend

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:48.170
— but what you should know about the sneaky
references is that some will set up the future

00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:49.930
of the Godzilla franchise.

00:07:49.930 --> 00:07:54.830
Actor O'Shea Jackson Jr. told Fandango during
a set visit in 2017 that he was, quote, "nerding

00:07:54.830 --> 00:07:58.500
out really hard" over the Easter eggs in King
of the Monsters, and said that fans will have

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:00.820
a blast trying to uncover them all.

00:08:00.820 --> 00:08:04.639
Director Michael Dougherty piggybacked off
Jackson Jr.'s remarks when he told Entertainment

00:08:04.639 --> 00:08:09.300
Weekly that the film will also tease the introduction
of another famous movie creature post-King

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:11.280
of the Monsters: King Kong.

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:12.280
Dougherty shared:

00:08:12.280 --> 00:08:15.370
"It's not like we're bending over backwards
to introduce Kong, but there's definitely

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:16.370
some bread crumbs."

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:21.160
Grab your binoculars and a basket before heading
out to see King of the Monsters, as the moviegoing

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:24.720
experience sounds like it will double as a
massive Easter egg hunt.

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:25.720
Shared cinematic universe

00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:28.510
Godzilla: King of the Monsters is no average
sequel.

00:08:28.510 --> 00:08:33.510
It expands the revived world that Godzilla
set up and calls back to the old-school monster

00:08:33.510 --> 00:08:38.320
movies produced by Toho, the Japanese company
responsible for 32 Godzilla films.

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:42.930
It also sets up a new cinematic universe packed
with monsters and centered on Monarch's undertakings

00:08:42.930 --> 00:08:45.330
that will stretch across multiple releases.

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:50.180
King of the Monsters not only serves as the
sequel to Godzilla, but also as the next entry

00:08:50.180 --> 00:08:55.050
in Warner Bros.' initial trio of MonsterVerse
movies, which see Godzilla exist among a wide

00:08:55.050 --> 00:08:58.990
variety of other giant super-monsters, new
and old.

00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:02.560
Additionally, director Michael Dougherty once
mentioned that King of the Monsters hinges

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:07.250
on something of a crossover event, as the
film unites the creatures featured in Toho's

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:08.250
classics.

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:10.060
Dougherty told the folks at Fandango:

00:09:10.060 --> 00:09:14.450
"Outside of the Universal classic monster
movies, Toho is one of the first companies

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:17.050
to pioneer the idea of a shared universe.

00:09:17.050 --> 00:09:19.450
They were doing it long before Marvel was.

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:23.290
Mothra was a completely separate film from
Godzilla when it started.

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:24.370
Same thing with Rodan.

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:28.130
So it kind of feels like things are coming
full circle [with King of the Monsters]."

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:29.130
A sequel

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:32.840
Before Godzilla: King of the Monsters even
released its first trailer, the bigwigs at

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:35.820
Warner Bros. and Legendary Pictures announced
plans for a sequel.

00:09:35.820 --> 00:09:40.620
You know, that third entry into the studios'
Godzilla trilogy, the last piece of the first

00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:44.930
wave of MonsterVerse movies, and the film
that King of the Monsters will tease with

00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:46.620
its references to King Kong?

00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:47.620
That one.

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:51.940
Aptly entitled Godzilla vs. Kong, the King
of the Monsters sequel has Death Note's Adam

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:55.580
Wingard on board as director, with many cast
members back in the fold.

00:09:55.580 --> 00:10:00.340
The plot of Godzilla vs. Kong will center
around a brutal brawl between Godzilla and

00:10:00.340 --> 00:10:02.130
the gorilla-like monster monkey.

00:10:02.130 --> 00:10:06.360
The film — which stars Alexander Skarsgård
as "the leader of a military unit" as well

00:10:06.360 --> 00:10:11.570
as Rebecca Hall, Jessica Henwick, Brian Tyree
Henry, and more — also focuses on humanity's

00:10:11.570 --> 00:10:13.060
fight for its future.

00:10:13.060 --> 00:10:16.630
Monarch's mission to discover the truth about
the Titans and a conspiracy that threatens

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:18.880
to end life on Earth continues

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:23.060
Make no mistake, though, there will be a clear
winner of the titular battle when it all goes

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:25.630
down on March 13th, 2020.

00:10:25.630 --> 00:10:27.040
As Wingard once confirmed:

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:32.120
"I do want people to walk away from this film
feeling like, 'Okay, there is a winner.'"

00:10:32.120 --> 00:10:34.680
"Long live the king."

